// Signing configuration for the app targets.
//
// This file is committed and must exist — the project references it as its
// base configuration. It deliberately carries nobody's Team ID: that is
// personal identity metadata, this fork is public, and a hardcoded value
// conflicts on every upstream merge that touches signing.
//
// To sign builds with your own identity, create `Local.xcconfig` beside this
// file (it is gitignored) containing:
//
//     OPENDISK_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//
// Find your Team ID with:
//
//     security find-certificate -c "Apple Development" -p \
//       | openssl x509 -noout -subject
//
// and read the OU= field — NOT the ID in parentheses after your email, which
// identifies the certificate rather than the team.
//
// Without a Local.xcconfig the project still builds and tests unsigned:
//
//     xcodebuild -scheme OpenDisk build CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO
//
// The leading "?" makes the include optional, so a fresh clone with no
// Local.xcconfig is not a build error.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"

// Empty unless Local.xcconfig sets it.
OPENDISK_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = $(OPENDISK_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM)
